WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.600
Chapter two: glass beads. And this time... you are Wren.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:13.666
West Africa, five hundred years ago. On the Gold Coast, a rare blue bead,

00:00:13.666 --> 00:00:18.199
the accori, could be worth its weight in gold. All were old.

00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:19.786
Nobody made new ones.

00:00:20.137 --> 00:00:25.247
Now you're a European trader. It's only glass, you think. I can make that!

00:00:25.247 --> 00:00:30.772
Europe's glassmakers tried. But people on the coast could tell the copies apart.

00:00:31.121 --> 00:00:33.869
New plan: ordinary beads, by the ton.

00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:38.917
By the late seventeen hundreds, Venice made tens of millions a year.

00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:44.189
In Liverpool, the price of one ounce of gold bought nearly fifty kilos.

00:00:44.189 --> 00:00:47.084
Coastal merchants still bargained hard.

00:00:47.435 --> 00:00:52.533
Ships from Liverpool carried them south, with cloth, iron and guns.

00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:57.099
They bought some gold and ivory, but mostly enslaved people.

00:00:57.099 --> 00:01:01.056
Glass beads helped pay for the Atlantic slave trade.

00:01:01.906 --> 00:01:06.853
Step off the ship. Imagine your family saved in ordinary beads:

00:01:06.853 --> 00:01:08.972
years of work, on a string.

00:01:08.972 --> 00:01:14.782
If every ship brings more beads, each one buys a little less. Same string.

00:01:14.782 --> 00:01:15.567
Less food.

00:01:15.918 --> 00:01:20.253
Unless the string held an accori. Nobody could copy those.

00:01:20.253 --> 00:01:23.392
Two hundred years on, a Dutch trader wrote

00:01:23.392 --> 00:01:26.307
it still traded for its weight in gold.

00:01:26.656 --> 00:01:29.670
Remember Ulm Hollow? Wren didn't steal.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:34.461
Wren just spent first, and pentaja savers paid the difference.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:39.253
When you're Wren, it feels like winning. Somebody always pays.

00:01:39.602 --> 00:01:44.256
Next: North America, where shell beads became money...

00:01:44.256 --> 00:01:46.583
until metal drills arrived.

